# GitHub MCP and CLI

When the user asks about **GitHub operations** (issues, pull requests, branches, repositories, users), prefer these tools in order:

## 1. GitHub MCP (preferred)

The GitHub MCP server (`github` or `user-github`) is configured at `https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/`. Use `call_mcp_tool` with server `github` (or `user-github` if that is the configured name).

**Before calling**: Check the tool schema/descriptor for required parameters (e.g. in `mcps/<server>/tools/` if available).

**Common MCP skills** (from [GitHub Copilot cheat sheet](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/reference/github-copilot-chat-cheat-sheet#mcp-skills)):

| Skill | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `create_branch` | Create branch in owner/repo |
| `create_or_update_file` | Add/update file on a branch |
| `push_files` | Push files to a branch |
| `update_pull_request_branch` | Update PR branch with base |
| `merge_pull_request` | Merge a PR |
| `get_me` | Current user info |
| `search_users` | Find users by name |

Plus: create issues, list PRs, retrieve repo info (exact tool names may vary; check schema).

## 2. GitHub CLI (`gh`) — fallback

When MCP is unavailable or for local/terminal workflows, use [GitHub CLI](https://cli.github.com/):

```bash
gh issue list          # List issues
gh pr status           # PR status for current branch
gh pr create           # Create PR
gh pr checkout <n>     # Checkout PR branch
gh repo view           # View repo README
gh release create      # Create release
```

## Quick decision

| Task | Prefer |
|------|--------|
| Create/merge PR, create branch, push files | GitHub MCP |
| List issues/PRs, search users, get repo info | GitHub MCP |
| Local git + GitHub (checkout PR, status) | `gh` CLI |
| MCP not responding | `gh` CLI |
